<div class="start-card"><p><strong>Requires:</strong> Products ready, Flyway applied and model probe passed.</p></div>
<details class="optional" id="trigger"><summary>How the Event Grid Blob trigger works</summary>
<p>{{file:apps/products-embedder/function_app.py}} declares a Blob trigger with <code>source='EventGrid'</code>. A BlobCreated notification reaches the Blob-extension webhook; the extension reads the private blob and passes an InputStream to Python. The path carries product/manual IDs.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="publish">Publish</h2>
{{snippet:commands.sh:embedder}}
<p>The stage builds the Python package remotely on Linux, publishes it, then registers the filtered Event Grid subscription. Flex Consumption supplies server-managed execution; the template supplies VNet access, identity-based host/deployment storage and telemetry.</p>
<h2 id="upload">Upload all three manuals</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Product name</th><th>Download</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Aurora Trail Lamp</td><td><a href="./samples/aurora-trail-lamp.txt" download>aurora-trail-lamp.txt</a></td></tr><tr><td>Cedar Desk Fan</td><td><a href="./samples/cedar-desk-fan.txt" download>cedar-desk-fan.txt</a></td></tr><tr><td>Harbor Travel Kettle</td><td><a href="./samples/harbor-travel-kettle.txt" download>harbor-travel-kettle.txt</a></td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>In Products → Upload product, submit each name/file. Expect <code>waiting → processing → ready</code>; intermediate states may be brief. Upload completion is not indexing completion.</p>
<h2 id="inspect">Inspect stored data</h2>
{{snippet:commands.sh:inspect-data}}
<div class="verification"><strong>Verification:</strong> all three manuals are ready, chunk counts are positive and min/max dimensions equal 1536. The inspection Job runs inside the VNet; it does not print full vectors.</div>
<h2 id="exercises">Make two changes</h2>
<ol><li>Copy Aurora's manual, change <code>420 lumens</code> to <code>510 lumens</code>, and label it revision B. Upload as a new product, "Aurora Trail Lamp Rev B". Compare each product's answer in the next chapter.</li><li>Activate the verification environment, run <code>python workshop/tools/replay_event.py</code>, then inspect counts again. Replaying a ready manual twice should add no chunks.</li></ol>
<details class="optional" id="chunks"><summary>Chunking and retry safety</summary><p>{{file:apps/shared/rag_core/chunks.py}} splits at text boundaries with bounded character counts/overlap. {{file:apps/shared/rag_core/models.py}} requests 1536-value embeddings. {{file:apps/shared/rag_core/embedding.py}} locks per manual, checks IDs/checksum, persists processing, then commits chunks + ready atomically.</p><p>A ready manual skips indexing. Duplicate Blob receipts may be suppressed before code runs; the database guard also prevents duplicates. Failed attempts persist errors and retry. Delivery is at-least-once; manuals are immutable.</p></details>
<details class="optional"><summary>Troubleshooting</summary><ul><li><strong>Still waiting:</strong> check subscription/filter and IndexManual discovery. For uploads made before subscription creation, upload a new product.</li><li><strong>No Function/key:</strong> check remote-build logs, extension bundle and host-storage roles: Blob Data Owner, Queue Data Contributor, Storage Account Contributor.</li><li><strong>Indexing failed:</strong> use the manual ID in Application Insights; check DB DNS, model identity/quota and dimensions.</li><li><strong>Delivery exhausted:</strong> inspect Event Grid's <code>event-deadletters</code> blobs separately from the Function host's <code>webjobs-blobtrigger-poison</code> queue.</li></ul></details>
